Two escape routes to a feasible finite check:
  (A) direct c=(k+1) lift small enough  -> works while k is small (n<=~12)
  (B) k+1 an ODD PRIME -> polynomial method skips the tight-tuple lift (Prop 4.1)

  n=10 (k=9):  route (A) -- small. DONE (Trakulthongchai 2025).
  n=11 (k=10): k+1=11 PRIME -> route (B). DONE.
  n=12 (k=11): k+1=12 composite, but still small enough for (A). DONE.
  n=13 (k=12): k+1=13 PRIME -> route (B) rescues the now-large lift. DONE.
  n=14 (k=13): k+1=14=2*7 composite -> (B) UNAVAILABLE; k=13 too big for (A). WALL.
